WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.225
IEC 62443 is a family of standards focused on cybersecurity for industrial automation and

00:00:06.225 --> 00:00:07.070
control systems.

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:11.935
These systems monitor or control physical processes in manufacturing, energy, water,

00:00:11.935 --> 00:00:14.595
transportation, buildings, and other operational environments.

00:00:14.595 --> 00:00:18.850
Their security must account for safety, availability, reliability, process integrity,

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:20.702
and long equipment lifecycles.

00:00:20.702 --> 00:00:23.970
The standards provide a structured way to discuss industrial cyber risk across

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:25.650
organizations and technical disciplines.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.715
They address security programs, system design, risk assessment, product development,

00:00:29.715 --> 00:00:33.000
technical capabilities, integration, and service delivery.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.920
IEC 62443 is therefore broader than a list of firewall settings or product features.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.295
Asset owners use the concepts to establish governance and determine what protection their

00:00:42.295 --> 00:00:43.280
operations require.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.520
Integrators translate those requirements into an architecture and commissioned system.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.965
Product suppliers build security capabilities into components and maintain secure

00:00:50.965 --> 00:00:52.612
development practices.

00:00:52.612 --> 00:00:55.920
Service providers support systems without weakening the controls around them.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.335
This division of responsibility matters because no single product can secure an industrial

00:01:00.335 --> 00:01:01.070
operation.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:02.920
A capable component can be configured poorly.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.000
A well-segmented system can be exposed through unmanaged remote access.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.545
Strong policy can fail if teams cannot produce evidence that controls are implemented and

00:01:11.545 --> 00:01:12.310
maintained.

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:14.820
IEC 62443 should be treated as a risk-based,

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.270
lifecycle-oriented framework for disciplined engineering.

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:21.275
It does not eliminate uncertainty or replace knowledge of the process.

00:01:21.275 --> 00:01:25.605
Its practical value comes from connecting organizational responsibility, architecture,

00:01:25.605 --> 00:01:27.490
technical requirements, verification,

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:31.200
and ongoing operation using a common industrial cybersecurity language.
